# Herald Core

- Module: `github.com/SolaTyolo/herald`. Project name: **Herald**.
- Channel providers: Traefik-style YAML routing; builtin only `smtp_email` / `inapp`; other channels are remote HTTP workers via `sdk/worker`. Do not add in-process plugin runtimes.
- `cmd/api` and `cmd/worker` must NOT import user provider implementations.
- Delivery: `routing.Table` + builtin SMTP / in_app; remote → `POST /delivery` + Redis result queue (default) or sync HTTP body.
- Persistence: `repository.Store` via `repository.Open()` — business layers use the Store port only.
- Missing records: use `repository.IsNotFound(err)`.
- Bootstrap roles: `RoleAPI` (migrations, bridge subscriber) vs `RoleWorker` (Asynq); same `PROVIDERS_CONFIG` and `REDIS_ADDR` on both.
- Worker SDK (`sdk/worker`) is for user Delivery Workers only; core does not import it.
- Minimize diff scope; match existing patterns.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
